<PARA INFOID = "T120025007" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Current Fuel Consumption Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0.0~30.0km/L</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Bar Graph Display</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer calculates and displays the current fuel consumption from the driving distance and fuel consumption for every 20 engine revolutions.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
<PARA INFOID = "T120025008" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Cumulative Average Fuel Consumption Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0.0~99.9km/L</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer calculates and displays the average fuel consumption from the accumulated driving distance and accumulated fuel injection volume since +B connection or reset.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>With the power source mode ON, the previous data is displayed. (After +B reconnection, 0.0km/L is displayed.)</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Reset Operation</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Pressing the DISP switch for approximately 0.8 seconds or more resets the cumulative average fuel consumption data.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
<PARA INFOID = "T120025009" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Cruising Range Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0~999km</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer calculates the fuel consumption from the engine speed, fuel injection volume, etc., and calculates and displays the cruising range from the current fuel level signal.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>With the power source mode ON, the previous data is displayed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
<PARA INFOID = "T120025010" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Cumulative Average Vehicle Speed Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0~300km/h</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The meter computer calculates and displays the cumulative average vehicle speed from the accumulated engine running time and accumulated driving distance since +B connection or reset.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>With the power source mode ON, the previous data is displayed. (After +B reconnection, 0km/h is displayed.)</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Reset Operation</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Pressing the DISP switch for approximately 0.8 seconds or more resets the cumulative average vehicle speed data.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
<PARA INFOID = "T120025011" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Cumulative Driving Time Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>0:00~99:59</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The clock in the combination meter accumulates and displays the time during which the engine is running.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When 99:59 is reached, the display continues from 0:00.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>With the power source mode ON, the previous data is displayed. (After +B reconnection, 0:00 is displayed.)</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, the display is blank (no display).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Reset Operation</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Pressing the DISP switch for approximately 0.8 seconds or more resets the cumulative driving time data.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
<PARA INFOID = "T120025012" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26Oct2009" INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Outside Temperature Display Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "16%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "83%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Display Range</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>-40~50℃</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The outside temperature data input from the ambient temperature sensor is corrected using the vehicle speed signal data input from the skid control computer, and a more accurate outside temperature is calculated and displayed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the outside temperature is below -40°C, -40°C is displayed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the outside temperature is 50°C or higher, 50°C is displayed.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>If a communication malfunction or input signal malfunction occurs, bars (--) are displayed.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>